./packs/claudinite-tasks/VERSIONS.md:15:| 60905.1 | 2026-09-05 | A task declares what its run does to pull requests and the executor resolves it once (#1695). `expected_outcome` grows to `no_code_changes` / `fresh_pr` / `amend_existing_or_create_new_pr` / `supersede_existing_pr`; the retired `none`/`pr` normalize at the door and `legacy-task-fields` advises the rename. `queue/target.mjs` resolves the branch and pull request between the precondition's go and code-work — a task's open pull requests recognised by the `claudinite/<pack>/<task>/` prefix or the `Claudinite-Task:` trailer on the head commit — and the executor hands it to code-work as `CLAUDINITE_TARGET_MODE`/`_BRANCH`/`_PR` and to the agent as `Target-branch:`/`Target-pr:`/`Supersedes:` fields; superseded pull requests close once the run's own exists (the executor after code-work, the session's converge otherwise), and a green unlanded incumbent is landed with the occurrence ending there. `deliverGenerated` takes the target as `branch`/`pr`, keeping its prefix discovery only under an executor that hands none in (#1698); `openDeliveredPull`/`disposeOpenPull` are deprecated on the same terms. `usage-fold` declares `amend_existing_or_create_new_pr`. |
./packs/claudinite-tasks/VERSIONS.md:18:| 60903.4 | 2026-09-03 | The task contract's tolerances, and the secrets bag's two, state the convergence window they end on instead of a count of who still declares them — a count nothing in the canon can take. `legacy-task-fields` says the same in its `why` (#1652). |
./packs/claudinite-tasks/VERSIONS.md:20:| 60903.2 | 2026-09-03 | The task contract's field and outcome tolerances stop describing themselves as permanent — they are accepted while members still declare them and no longer, which is what `legacy-task-fields` and #1642 are for. `SESSION_SCOPES` gains the removal link it was missing beside the advisory it already had (#1637). |
./packs/claudinite-tasks/VERSIONS.md:21:| 60903.1 | 2026-09-03 | `legacy-task-fields` — an advisory over a repo's own `tasks/<name>/task.mjs` for the retired field names (`agent_preprocessing*`, `prework*`, `after`) and the one-word outcome ceilings, read from the declaration source because the contract's door normalizes them away before anything downstream can see them (#1637). |
